include g474.tdc
diagram c2 "Tail: the edge comes while the main thread wakes"
letter "C2"
num value "up to 1662 cycles"
num share "part of 0.024 %"
num path "direct ISR, idle, poll 100 ms"
num arch "PendSV (USE_SWITCH=n)"
what "Every 100 ms the main thread wakes to check for the end of the run. The SysTick ISR makes it ready, PendSV switches to it, it calls k_msleep() again, and PendSV switches back to the idle thread. Many of these steps hold BASEPRI. An edge in a masked part waits until the mask drops."
evidence "About 3160 masked cycles per main-thread wake (poll 10 ms point), against about 900 for a bare SysTick event."
evidence "The longest masked section that an edge hit is about 1620 cycles (max 1662 minus the floor 41), about 9.5 µs."
evidence "With a busy thread and time slicing, the slice expiry adds more of these sections: max 2056 cycles."
src "irq-baseline-1m/20261024T155016Z, irq-checks-1m/20261024T163216Z"

axis "cycles after the edge" -1400..1700

idle sleep -1400..-1320 "WFI"
dev pending 0..140 "pending" : Masked by BASEPRI. As soon as PendSV restores BASEPRI, the EXTI0 IRQ preempts it (PendSV has the lowest priority).
idle sleep 1410..1700 "WFI"
mask -1280..-540 "BASEPRI"
mask -470..140 "BASEPRI"
mask 420..760 "BASEPRI"
mask 1030..1380 "BASEPRI"
at -1300
tick 780 "announce, ready main" : The main thread's k_msleep() timeout expires. The ISR makes the thread ready and pends PendSV.
at -500
pendsv 640 "switch idle → main" : z_arm_pendsv: BASEPRI is set from swap_helper.S:123 to :264.
hw 26 : Exception entry, preempting PendSV.
dev miss 20 : Cold cache after the timer and switch code.
dev 6 : The ISR reads TIM2->CNT.
at 200
pendsv 40 : PendSV finishes.
at 250
main 750 "k_msleep() again" : The main thread checks for the end of the run and sleeps again: it adds a timeout and calls the scheduler, with locks.
at 1010
pendsv 390 "main → idle" : Switch back to the idle thread.

@t0_1 tick "SysTick IRQ" at -1300
@t0_2 edge "edge" at 0
@t0_3 stamp "CNT read" at 192
span 0..192 "example: 192 cycles"
